        <mxCell id="eKk8V9CFJGvcSFXkHoSS-39" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font color=&quot;#ff0000&quot;&gt;Both properties are read only&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="66" width="130" x="-180" y="650" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eKk8V9CFJGvcSFXkHoSS-43" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(255, 0, 0), rgb(255, 144, 144));&quot;&gt;Implementation, current cannot pass through it&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="66" width="130" x="300" y="1130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eKk8V9CFJGvcSFXkHoSS-44" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(255, 0, 0), rgb(255, 144, 144));&quot;&gt;Maybe further event on interface and base class so it can be raised when internal connectivity is changed (Switch)&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="66" width="130" x="-320" y="650" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eKk8V9CFJGvcSFXkHoSS-45" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(255, 0, 0), rgb(255, 144, 144));&quot;&gt;No grouping per circuit, merely evaluate from each power source&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="66" width="130" x="850" y="751" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eKk8V9CFJGvcSFXkHoSS-47" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(255, 0, 0), rgb(255, 144, 144));&quot;&gt;Have wires and electrical devices register themselves to the circuit solver so it works even for those spawning at runtime&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="66" width="130" x="710" y="1100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eKk8V9CFJGvcSFXkHoSS-65" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(255, 0, 0), rgb(255, 144, 144));&quot;&gt;Static accessor, singleton pattern&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="130" x="840" y="830" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eKk8V9CFJGvcSFXkHoSS-67" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(255, 0, 0), rgb(255, 144, 144));&quot;&gt;isDirty set to true if any connected/disconnected events from wires arise, resulting in the need to re-evaluate the circuit, if nothing happens we don&#39;t need to unnecessarily re-evaluate. If isDirty we run in LateUpdate to evaluate circuit&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="320" x="860" y="910" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eKk8V9CFJGvcSFXkHoSS-68" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(255, 0, 0), rgb(255, 144, 144));&quot;&gt;isDirty begins as true since we need to evaluate once at start up too and also set to true when devices/wires are registered and unregistered.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="320" x="860" y="1010" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eKk8V9CFJGvcSFXkHoSS-69" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(255, 0, 0), rgb(255, 144, 144));&quot;&gt;Set isDirty false at the beginning of EvaluateCircuit so we dont lose isDirty state if other events come in while evaluating.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="320" x="870" y="1080" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eKk8V9CFJGvcSFXkHoSS-70" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(255, 0, 0), rgb(255, 144, 144));&quot;&gt;Make a traversal method that takes a starting terminal and has a return of the list of electrical devices it reached. Call it for both the positive and negative terminals for the power source device.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(255, 0, 0), rgb(255, 144, 144));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(255, 0, 0), rgb(255, 144, 144));&quot;&gt;Then if the device is on both lists, we know it was reached otherwise it was not and can appropriately PowerOn/Off and because we have a safe guard it will prevent a powered on device from power on again and vice versa.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We should keep track of visited terminals so that we do not continue in an infinite loop&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="320" x="870" y="1230" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="taW5MygLJuY6vMWt_g4N-1" parent="1" style="swimlane;fontStyle=0;childLayout=stackLayout;horizontal=1;startSize=40;fillColor=#ffff88;horizontalStack=0;resizeParent=1;resizeParentMax=0;resizeLast=0;collapsible=1;marginBottom=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeColor=#36393d;" value="&lt;div&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;lt;Enumeration&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b&gt;WireEnd&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="92" width="120" x="785" y="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
